# Web deploy (Vercel)

## Why prod looked “only on my PC”

- **`vercel --prod`** uploads **whatever is on disk** (including **uncommitted** edits). That production URL can differ from what anyone else gets from Git.
- **Git-connected Vercel** builds from **`main` on GitHub**. Other devices and teammates only see changes after **`git push origin main`** and a successful Vercel deploy for that commit.

Using CLI prod without pushing the same commit (or pushing without waiting for the Git deploy) causes **two production truths**.

## Required workflow (default)

The agent runs this **automatically** when work is done (`auto-commit-deploy.mdc`) — not only when the user says “배포해”.

1. Finish the feature on **`main`** (or merge to `main`).
2. **Commit** everything that should be live (never rely on dirty working tree for “배포 완료”).
3. **`git push origin main`**.
4. Confirm the **Vercel deployment for that commit** is Ready (Git integration — do not assume local `vercel --prod` replaced it).

## Do not

- Run **`vercel --prod`** as the only deploy step when the user asked for **everyone** to see the change.
- Run **`vercel --prod`** with **uncommitted** changes unless the user explicitly wants a one-off preview prod and understands Git prod will differ until pushed.
- Tell the user “배포 완료” after only a local CLI deploy without **push + Git deploy** confirmation.

## When CLI prod is OK

- User explicitly asks for **`vercel --prod`**, **and** the same tree is **committed and pushed to `main`** immediately after (same commit SHA on Git and Vercel).

## Build

- Production build command: `npm run vercel-build` (see `vercel.json`).
